    "title": "Germantown crowns winners of Running of the Weenies race - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Vivian Nguyen ,\n9 hours ago MEMPHIS, Tenn. -- The City of Germantown named the winners of the Running of the Weenies race, along with the best-dressed weenie, on Saturday.\nSixty-six Dachshunds raced to the finish line while 14 stylish pups competed for Best Dressed Hot Dog at the Germantown Festival.\nWinner of best dressed Courtesy of City of Germantown Winner of best dressed Courtesy of City of Germantown Winner of best dressed Courtesy of City of Germantown Clara, owned by Mandy Hurdle, dressed as the one and only Tennessee icon Dolly Parton.\n1st place of running of the weenies Courtesy of City of Germantown Courtesy of City of Germantown The race winners include the following:\n1st: Loie, owned by Matt Wukasch\n2nd: Zula, owned by Baran and Helen Carter\n3rd: Poe, owned by Casen Knight and Amanda Miller\n\"Congratulations to all of our winners and every Dachshund who took to the track!\" said the city of Germantown.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WREG.com.",
    "summary": "9 hours ago MEMPHIS, Tenn. -- The City of Germantown named the winners of the Running of the Weenies race, along with the best-dressed weenie, on Saturday. Sixty-six Dachshunds raced to the finish line while 14 stylish pups competed for Best Dressed Hot Dog at the Germantown Festival. Winner of best dressed Courtesy of City of Germantown Winner of best dressed Courtesy of City of Germantown Winner of best dressed Courtesy of City of Germantown Clara, owned by Mandy Hurdle, dressed as the one and only Tennessee icon Dolly Parton.",
